course: dictionary
lesson: 13808
title: Abbreviations: letters that stand for words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer word or phrase, and its letters stand for the words it is made from. «IQ» is an abbreviation: the letters I and Q stand for intelligence quotient. Read the words around it to check what it means.
explain: «Maya scored well on the puzzle test, so her teacher said she had a high IQ.» The words scored well and high tell you that IQ is a score that shows how clever someone is at certain thinking skills. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a high intelligence quotient" still makes sense.
explain: Be careful, because an abbreviation can hide a meaning bigger than its letters. «The IQ test had patterns and puzzles, but it did not test kindness.» Many scientists say an IQ score measures only some skills, not everything that makes a person good or wise.
fact: IQ stands for intelligence quotient.
fact: An IQ score comes from a special test that tries to measure some thinking skills, like puzzles and patterns.
fact: The average IQ score is set at 100.
fact: Scientists say an IQ score does not measure kindness, creativity or wisdom.
fact: IQ scores can change with schooling.
exercise: What does IQ stand for? | Internet quality | Interesting questions | Itchy quiet | *Intelligence quotient
exercise: «Maya got a high IQ score on the puzzle test.» What does a high IQ score suggest? | *The person is good at some thinking skills, like puzzles | The person lost the test | The person is the tallest in the class | The person has the best handwriting
exercise: The average IQ score is set at what number? | 10 | 1000 | *100 | 50
test: Scientists say an IQ score does not measure what? | *Kindness | Thinking quickly | Patterns | Puzzle skills
test: «The school gave the class an IQ test on patterns.» What kind of test is it? | A test of every skill a person has | A cooking test | A test of running speed | *A test of some thinking skills
exam: What does the abbreviation IQ tell a reader? | A short name for a large city | *A score from a test that tries to measure some thinking skills | A type of bread from the school canteen | A sport played with a ball
